-- A natDiv or natMod in a shader needs a closed divisor above 0: in WGSL
-- x % 0u is x, but in the C evaluator it is a trap. The divisor here is never
-- 0, but the writer cannot see that.
def modE : Tile 2 2 U32 -> Tile 2 2 U32 := fun t => tabulate 2 2 (fun i j => at t (natMod i (natAdd j 1)) 0)
